  "notes": [
    "Reflexive compound of *tener* — follows the same irregular patterns throughout, just like *mantenerse*, *contenerse*, *sostenerse*.",
    "Irregular yo present: *me detengo* (go-verb), with e→ie stem change in tú/él/ellos forms (te detienes, se detiene, se detienen); nosotros keeps the unstressed stem (nos detenemos).",
    "Irregular preterite stem: *detuv-* (me detuve, te detuviste, se detuvo...).",
    "Irregular future/conditional stem: *detendr-* (me detendré, me detendría).",
    "Subjuntivo built from the yo stem: *deteng-* (me detenga, te detengas...).",
    "Past participle is regular: **detenido**.",
    "Imperativo tú affirmative is irregular, following *tener→ten*: *detente* (not the expected \"detiénete\"). Usted/nosotros/ustedes affirmative forms attach the reflexive pronoun to the subjuntivo form with a written accent to preserve stress (deténgase, detengámonos, deténganse); negative forms place the pronoun separately in front (no te detengas...).",
    "*¡Detente! No cruces la calle.* (\"Stop! Don't cross the street.\")",
    "*El coche se detuvo en el semáforo.* (\"The car stopped at the traffic light.\")",
    "Related: *detener* (non-reflexive, \"to stop/detain someone or something\"), *la detención* (detention/stop, noun), *pararse* (synonym, \"to stop oneself\")."
  ],
  "sourceFile": "Verbs/d/Detenerse.md"
